Z||000000||MickeyAsh||12-06-2001||02:26 AM||||Hey guys, looking at a N* conversion coming up (hopefully, since I threw a rod in the 6er I dont wanna sink any money into it), and I've almost got my hands on an entire caddy to use for a donor... my question is, is there any way to yank the PS off the donor caddy and fit it to the Fiero? And if someone has done it, I'd love some pics...||||reg||5
Z||000001||artherd||12-06-2001||04:09 AM||||Not that our cars really need it, but I suppose you could use the stock pump on the engine, run some lines up front, and swap in a suitable power rack...<P>There are some racks that almost bolt right in, but off the top of my head I can't think of them!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||MickeyAsh||12-06-2001||02:00 PM||||Doesn't seem like it'd be that difficult of a thing to do... maybe I'm just naive, but I keep thinking back to when everyone kept saying how difficult a set of 12"s behind my seats would be to install... well it took me two months of working hard at my leisure, but overall I wouldn't call it extemely difficult... if I had the opportunity, I'd do it again, just with some shallower 12"s or 10"s... back to the N* though, what all is involved in the Pwr Steering system that would require being moved from the donor to the Fiero?||||reg||1
